comments[18]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T02:42:14.362Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete3134-item all-status full strict read has zero unreadable items or omissions. Request-specific search and open/in-progress inventories found no missing-interpreter or negative-replay owner. pm-gh1604 is completed for missing executables, so this bounded follow-up owns new review work; pm-gh1607 and pm-lifecycle-example-scope retain their completed lineage. PR1608 review threads4384464587,4384464563,4384464571."
  "2026-10-27T02:46:18.309Z","harness:codex","Native reproduction: executable lookup succeeds, but /bin/sh reports absent shebang interpreter with exit126 and the original bad-interpreter diagnostic on this host. The real linked regression failed as assertion_failure before this change (negative log retained privately), then passed after the fix. POSIX shells reporting named not-found/127 use the same bounded-header proof; Windows resolution remains separate. Linux execve documents ENOENT for a missing script interpreter: https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/execve.2.html. The classifier reads at most256 header bytes with nonblocking open, closes the handle, declines incomplete/ambiguous or unavailable evidence, and never reruns the user command. Real executed scripts spoofing both127 and126 diagnostics remain assertions. Focused110 tests pass, including platform controls; focused exact module coverage is100/100/100/100 (42statements,45branches,6functions,37lines), typecheck and focused lint pass."
  "2026-10-27T02:49:11.012Z","harness:codex","Review1608 negative-control clarification: candidate73846f26f2255ca4afaffb642543e2e3d3d63f44 with ONLY src/sdk/test/command-resolution.ts replaced by 9dad0a28c87beb0fbb66f9eec9f7360f9bf549dd. The recorded runnable control archives immutable source into a disposable checkout, uses sandboxed PM roots, and requires exactly the named AssertionError before intentionally returning exit1; setup/runtime failure returns3. Executed now and proved the intended failure. Current passing local_checks are separate. Existing immutable events remain preserved; no prior history was edited."
  "2026-10-27T02:49:45.963Z","harness:codex","Acceptance complete: linked execution passed all110 tests; focused exact coverage passed100/100/100/100 with zero uncovered counts; typecheck, focused ESLint, and docs/skills gate pass. Each of the three replay controls independently archived its immutable candidate, substituted only the named pre-fix source file, and proved exactly its intended AssertionError. The current fields identify runnable failing controls separately from current passing local_checks, while old immutable history is preserved. The dependency checkpoint finding is declined with exact timestamps in its existing inline thread: checkpoint22:07:37Z predates PR creation23:33:40Z. Hosted revised-head checks and review remain required before merge."
  "2026-10-27T03:03:13.745Z","harness:codex","Current-head static run40440955981 job121981248330 failed the zero-tolerance absence guard: the new interpreter lookup catches ENOENT without ENOTDIR. Dependency, repository static, token, context, docs and defect evidence assertions in that admission passed. Reopened only this actively edited follow-up to use the existing canonical filesystem absence predicate, add the ENOTDIR boundary control, and rerun meaningful local acceptance. No policy ceiling will change."
  "2026-10-27T03:04:09.727Z","harness:codex","The first reopen invocation used an unsupported reason flag and did not mutate state. The positional-reason reopen and normal claim/start then succeeded, preserving the previous closure archive. Active work now uses the canonical isFileAbsentError helper for ENOENT and ENOTDIR, with a new ENOTDIR boundary case. No force or absence-policy exception is used."
  "2026-10-27T03:06:28.489Z","harness:codex","Absence refinement:111 focused/linked tests pass, including ENOTDIR and actual absent-interpreter scripts; focused exact coverage remains100/100/100/100 with zero uncovered counts. The canonical absence-tolerance guard passes at its unchanged zero ceiling, typecheck and lint pass. Current Node and Bun public-SDK consumers independently classify the script as spawn_error, retain native126, and match exact stderr. Current-source sampled Sentry pm history root/trace is fresh at02:58:23UTC with a25.48ms span; independent telemetry start/finish ingestion is0.522995s/0.051558s. Expanded scoped observation from21:00UTC has241starts/240finishes with the same one unequal pair; physical queues are empty. Existing partial-pairing investigation remains separate and no universal pairing claim is made."
  "2026-10-27T03:07:29.370Z","harness:codex","The241/240 pairing observation above ends at03:00:30UTC. A later query while the linked test command was still active also saw that in-flight start, which is not a missing terminal event. The earlier unequal changelog session identity is confirmed. The broad local repository-assurance attempt passed static, absence, token, context, docs and defect assertions but rejected a stale cached advisory receipt. Refreshing the normal feed receipt before repeating that read-only assurance; no dependency acceptance is inferred from a stale receipt."
  "2026-10-27T03:09:56.747Z","harness:codex","Refreshed normal registry/OSV advisory evidence passes; the full local repository-static-quality assurance now passes every assertion, including its unchanged absence ceiling.111 linked tests, focused exact100/100/100/100 coverage, typecheck, lint and Node/Bun public SDK consumers pass on the canonical-helper refinement. Earlier failed hosted static and stale-receipt local attempts remain preserved. Final revised-head required checks and full free-tier review are mandatory before merge."
  "2026-10-27T03:35:06.564Z","harness:codex","Full-review correction: installed Vitest4.1.12 JSON reporter stores suite-level runtime errors in testResults[].message and does not emit numRuntimeErrorTestSuites. The current runnable negative control requires every suite message to be exactly empty, alongside the single named AssertionError and native exit1. This corrected immutable-source replay was executed and proved the intended failure. A missing, nonempty or malformed suite message refuses proof. Existing historical events remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-27T03:35:44.918Z","harness:codex","All111 linked tests and current-source hosted CI40442741640 pass at8bedb5f771be697dffacb3397f55565a429be9f6, including exact aggregate100/100/100/100 coverage with zero uncovered counts, static, native Windows and all six packed first-run legs. Full review found no production-code issue and two evidence improvements: refresh the source receipt on the lifecycle owner, and use actual Vitest4 suite-message error data. All three corrected immutable-source negative controls execute and prove their intended assertion failure. Production source and tests have not changed since the accepted8bed head; pending final metadata checks/review remain pre-merge requirements."
  "2026-10-27T05:02:02.568Z","harness:codex","Release-base reconciliation: AutoRelease advanced main to77ff26ad72e141de7c3f56dfddc6ff7951dafab4 and created tagv2026.10.27 while the PR waited for runners. A normal merge preserves published history. Latest pm-changelog2026.10.26 regenerated the file and correctly retains all six delivery changes in Unreleased, with the tagged27 base inventory in its own dated section. No package bug or hand-edited changelog workaround is used. The branch inherits release-version metadata27; runtime implementation and tests remain unchanged from accepted8bed. Build succeeds and pm version reports2026.10.27. New exact-head checks/review remain mandatory, and tag creation is separate from npm publication."
  "2026-10-27T05:08:18.717Z","harness:codex","The queued259 static job122008784709 finally ran after tag27 appeared and correctly rejected its pre-tag changelog as out of date. The locally merged release base and package-generated changelog now pass the check. Contract snapshot, public SDK snapshot with zero classified changes, plugin wrapper/skill generation checks, Node/Bun public SDK consumers, tracker-context quality, graph composition, record integrity and defect evidence all pass on the inherited27 metadata. The six pending changes remain Unreleased. This is release-base reconciliation, with no source implementation or assertion change."
  "2026-10-27T05:55:57.845Z","harness:codex","Complete six-item control audit: the original executable, history-recency and serial-allocation fields also used passing checks. They now pin frozen candidateaff043f08ea0bd4a14b30af6f420d0f7f01c910f with only pre-fix execution.ts, an explicit newestFirst=false projection mutant, or pre-fix vitest.config.ts, respectively. All three reproduce exactly their expected named assertion with empty suite errors. The prior lifecycle, scoped-example and direct-interpreter controls were independently re-executed and proved too: all six now have distinct unsafe conditions and expected exit1 versus refusal3. The first serial evidence predicate refused a truncated Vitest message; matching its observed unique filename prefix now proves the correct guard without relaxing the test. No runtime implementation, assertions, deadlines or ceilings changed. Exact-aff CodeFactor and DeepScan evidence is releasable with zero issues/annotations; revised metadata-head CI/review remain required."
  "2026-10-27T06:27:53.394Z","harness:codex","Accepted review4385717216 on source7ea191db9400e68b2a76ce74d7f5d9d5da06eab8: add the POSIX eligible-status guard before stderr splitting. Windows already short-circuits its eligible statuses. Reuse this canonical item, retain existing executable/interpreter semantics and pinned negative controls, and rerun linked verification before close/release. Only this implementation is active."
  "2026-10-27T06:34:44.681Z","harness:codex","Review4385717216 remediation: POSIX ineligible exit statuses now return before splitting stderr; Windows retains its existing short circuit. The linked CLI run passes all111 tests across command-resolution36, native missing-command2 and test-command73. Focused source coverage passes44/44 statements,49/49 branches,6/6 functions and38/38 lines, zero uncovered; build and focused ESLint pass. No new test, assertion, timeout, retry or resolver contract was introduced. All six independently executed pinned negative controls remain valid core-regression proof; final hosted checks and a fresh full review of the new head remain required before merge."
  "2026-10-27T06:34:45.503Z","harness:codex","Release boundary verified live on 2026-10-27: daily AutoRelease40445899486 succeeded; public npm and GitHub Release v2026.10.27 are available. An independent isolated-cache verifier passes all four bins, real npx and bunx CLI/default dispatch, MCP stateless Skills/Apps and HTTP discovery plus missing-bin/command controls. Independent npm and Bun exact-package installations each complete the13-step agent acceptance journey. This tagged base does not contain the six PR1608 changes: those remain Unreleased in the package-generated changelog. There is no extra automatic release or manual publish request in this delivery."
  "2026-10-27T08:32:41.618Z","harness:codex","Daily deduplication verified live: morning_dispatcher40445899486 succeeded, then native_schedule40472638505 at08:18:55UTC succeeded by selecting the existing v2026.10.27 tag, verifying completed Release40449393972 and its public npm/GitHub publication before any preparation work. Its log08:19:25..32UTC confirms reuse of77ff26ad72e141de7c3f56dfddc6ff7951dafab4; no second version was prepared/published. GitHub matching refs contain exactly refs/tags/v2026.10.27. These are two producer invocations and one automatic release. The PR changes remain unpublished and no manual release was requested."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T05:55:57.251Z","harness:codex","Audit every delivery negative control, rather than only the latest review location: pin a pre-fix source file or explicit unsafe mutant and distinguish the expected assertion failure from passing checks and setup refusals. Vitest4.1.12 reports suite errors in testResults[].message and may truncate expected values in assertion stacks; combine the exact named test, AssertionError, a stable unique matcher fragment where needed, and empty suite messages. Reproduce in disposable archives with sandboxed PM roots, and preserve old immutable events when strengthening current evidence."
